{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-8828",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We divide both sides of the equation by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and use the identity $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-\\frac{2\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}} & =0 \\\\ 5\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}-2 & =0 \\\\ 5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5})=0.380\\,506…≈0.380\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places. \n\nSince $0.380\\,5$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=0.380\\,5.$\n\nTo find the other solution in the given interval, we add $\\pi $ to the principal value. Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=0.380\\,506…+\\pi =3.522\\,099…≈3.522\\,1\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places. \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}≈0.380\\,5\\cdot 3.522\\,1≈1.3\n$$\n\nrounded to one decimal place.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
